#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
genesi-ai-video — local video generation for Genesi AI Mode.

The AI Mode Monitor's Video page is a front end over this tool, the same split
as genesi-ai-image and its Image page: models, downloads, the engine and the
GPU live here, where they can be run and tested from a terminal, and the
window only draws what this prints. With --json every subcommand prints one
JSON object per line on stdout; human text goes to stderr.

    genesi-ai-video status    [--json]
    genesi-ai-video catalog   [--json]
    genesi-ai-video pull      MODEL [--variant V] [--json]
    genesi-ai-video remove    MODEL [--variant V] [--json]
    genesi-ai-video generate  --model MODEL [--variant V] --prompt TEXT
                              [--mode t2v|i2v|flf2v|r2v|v2v|extend]
                              [--image START_OR_REFERENCE] [--end-image END]
                              [--video SOURCE] [--seconds S | --frames N]
                              [--size 480p|720p] [--aspect 16:9|9:16|1:1]
                              [--steps N] [--cfg C] [--seed S] [--negative TEXT]
                              [--lora ID[:WEIGHT]]... [--turbo]
                              [--low-memory] [--light-vae]
                              [--out PATH] [--keep-llm] [--json]
    genesi-ai-video lora      list|import FILE [--name N] [--trigger WORDS]
                              |remove ID [--json]
    genesi-ai-video gallery   [--limit N] [--json]

── Why it is built on genesi-ai-image ──────────────────────────────────────

Same engine (stable-diffusion.cpp, `sd-cli -M vid_gen`), same model folder,
same download-resume-verify path, same LoRA store, same out-of-memory retry.
So this tool LOADS genesi-ai-image as a module and adds only what is video:
the catalog, the frame and size rules, the extra inputs (end frame, control
video, a video to continue), and turning the engine's output into something
a person can play and share. A fix to downloads or LoRAs lands in both pages
at once, and the image catalog is never touched by anything here.

── What the modes are ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  t2v     text to video.
  i2v     image to video: the picture is the FIRST FRAME. The face in it is
          the face in the video -- the most faithful way to animate a person.
  flf2v   first and last frame: the video travels from one to the other.
  r2v     a reference (VACE): a person or object from a photo appears in a
          NEW scene, not as the first frame.
  v2v     restyle a video (VACE): its frames steer the new one, so motion and
          composition stay while the look follows the prompt.
  extend  continue a video: its last frame starts a new image-to-video run,
          and the two are joined. Repeat it to go longer than one run allows.

v2v and extend need ffmpeg (to read the source video). Output is the engine's
MJPG .avi, turned into an H.264 .mp4 when ffmpeg is installed.

── Turbo ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

For video, Turbo is a distillation LoRA (Wan Lightning / LightX2V / Turbo):
4 to 6 steps instead of 20 to 30, at cfg 1. Unlike pictures there is no warm
server: a clip takes minutes, and the load is a small part of that.
"""
